          <ul class="checkpoint-list">
            <li>
              <span class="ck-icon">🗺️</span>
              <div class="ck-text">
                <strong>ODD Coverage Evidence Matrix</strong>
                <span>Build a test scenario matrix with rows = ODD dimensions (weather × lighting × road type × speed range) and columns = performance metrics (precision, recall, F1, latency). Every cell must have test results. Cells with insufficient data are compliance gaps — document them explicitly in the Technical File with a closure plan and date.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ck-icon">🛡️</span>
              <div class="ck-text">
                <strong>Robustness &amp; Adversarial Testing (Art. 15)</strong>
                <span>Required test categories: (1) sensor degradation — rain/mud occlusion, sensor noise injection; (2) adversarial inputs — patch attacks on camera, spoofed radar returns; (3) distribution shift — geographies and weather not in training data; (4) edge cases — occluded pedestrians, unusual vehicle types, construction zones. Document pass/fail thresholds in the Technical File before testing begins, not after.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ck-icon">👁️</span>
              <div class="ck-text">
                <strong>Human Oversight Verification (Art. 14)</strong>
                <span>Verify and document: (1) driver override latency ≤ defined threshold (typically 200ms for safety-critical decisions); (2) system provides interpretable output sufficient for driver intervention — confidence score, decision class, and trigger reason must be accessible; (3) override events are logged with cause code per Art. 12 schema; (4) system degrades gracefully when human is not monitoring (SOTIF requirement).</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ck-icon">📦</span>
              <div class="ck-text">
                <strong>V&amp;V Evidence Packaging for Notified Body</strong>
                <span>Assemble the validation evidence package: ODD coverage matrix (signed PDF or structured JSON), robustness test report with raw results, human oversight verification report, and updated Technical File linking each test to the relevant Annex IV section. Version the package as a release artifact in your repo. The notified body needs to trace from a test result back to the Technical File entry in under 5 minutes — structure accordingly.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="ck-icon">📊</span>
              <div class="ck-text">
                <strong>Statistical Significance Requirements</strong>
                <span>Performance claims in the Technical File require statistical backing. Minimum: 95% confidence intervals on all primary metrics, sample size justification per ODD slice, and a statement on the minimum detectable effect size. Claims without confidence intervals will be challenged in a conformity assessment. Document this in Annex IV §2.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="alert alert-warn" style="margin-top:20px;">
            <span class="alert-icon">⚠️</span>
